      "taskType": "errorAnalysis",
      "prompt": "In a model, t is elapsed time, so $t\\ge0$. A student proposes $t={{candidate}}$ for $\\log_2(t+{{offset}})={{n}}$ and says it is reasonable because it satisfies the logarithmic equation. Check the original equation AND the context, then repair the student's verdict.",
      "stimulus": {
        "kind": "steps",
        "title": "Student's reasoning",
        "steps": [
          {
            "id": "algebra",
            "label": "Equation check",
            "work": "The log argument is positive and the logarithm equals {{n}}."
          },
          {
            "id": "claim",
            "label": "Student conclusion",
            "work": "Therefore t={{candidate}} is a reasonable model solution."
          }
        ]
      },
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "argument",
          "label": "Original log argument",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "expected": "{{power}}"
        },
        {
          "id": "lhs",
          "label": "Original left side",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "expected": "{{n}}"
        },
        {
          "id": "algebra",
          "label": "Algebraic equation status",
          "inputProfile": "choice",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "valid",
              "label": "The candidate satisfies the logarithmic equation."
            },
            {
              "id": "invalid",
              "label": "The candidate does not satisfy the logarithmic equation."
            }
          ],
          "expected": "valid"
        },
        {
          "id": "context",
          "label": "Context check",
          "inputProfile": "choice",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "invalid",
              "label": "The candidate violates $t\\ge0$."
            },
            {
              "id": "valid",
              "label": "The candidate is allowed by $t\\ge0$."
            }
          ],
          "expected": "invalid"
        },
        {
          "id": "verdict",
          "label": "Corrected reasonableness verdict",
          "inputProfile": "choice",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "reject",
              "label": "Reject — algebraically valid but unreasonable in the time context."
            },
            {
              "id": "keep",
              "label": "Keep — satisfying the equation overrides the context restriction."
            }
          ],
          "expected": "reject"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "Reasonableness can require both algebraic validity and contextual validity.",
        "reasoning": [
          "At t={{candidate}}, the argument is {{power}}>0 and $\\log_2({{power}})={{n}}$, so the logarithmic equation is true.",
          "But t={{candidate}} is negative, violating the elapsed-time restriction.",
          "The student's final verdict must be corrected: the solution is algebraically valid but unreasonable for this model."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "Reject t={{candidate}} in context."
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Keep the algebraic and contextual checks separate; a candidate can pass one and fail the other."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "Elapsed time cannot be negative even if the logarithmic equation itself is satisfied."
      ],
      "generator": {
        "parameters": {
          "n": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 1,
            "max": 3
          },
          "gap": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 1,
            "max": 4
          }
        },
        "derived": {
          "power": "pow(2,n)",
          "offset": "power+gap",
          "candidate": "-gap"
        }
      }
    }
